<section class="mx-auto max-w-readable px-5 py-12">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
    Version <%= privacyVersion %> · Last updated <%= updated %>
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-900">
    MamaTriage is a <strong>research prototype</strong> built for an MSc project at MIVA
    Open University, Abuja. It is not a medical service and is not a commercial product.
  </div>

  <div class="prose mt-8 space-y-8 text-slate-700">

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">In short</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>We ask for a name to call you. Nothing else is required.</li>
        <li>If you choose Telegram, <strong>we never ask for your phone number</strong>.</li>
        <li>If you choose WhatsApp, your number is scrambled before it is stored and is
            never kept in a form anyone can read.</li>
        <li>Your conversations are stored with identifying details removed, so the system
            can be checked and improved.</li>
        <li>You can stop at any time, and ask us to delete your data.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">What we collect</h2>

      <table class="mt-3 w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-slate-300 text-left">
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold text-ink">What</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold text-ink">Why</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">The name you give us</td>
            <td class="py-2">So we can greet you. A nickname is fine.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">Which channel you chose</td>
            <td class="py-2">So we know where to reply.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">
              A <strong>scrambled</strong> version of your phone number or chat ID
            </td>
            <td class="py-2">
              So we can recognise you across messages. It cannot be turned back into your
              number.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">Your messages, with identifying details removed</td>
            <td class="py-2">
              To check whether the advice given was clinically appropriate.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">The urgency level the system decided, and why</td>
            <td class="py-2">To measure whether the system is safe and accurate.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">What we do not collect</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>
          Your phone number in readable form — unless you ask for text reminders, which is
          the one exception and is explained below.
        </li>
        <li>Any phone number at all, if you register on Telegram and do not want text
            reminders.</li>
        <li>Your address, date of birth, or any identity document.</li>
        <li>Your location.</li>
        <li>Anything from your phone beyond the messages you send us.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <strong>If you ask for text reminders.</strong> A text message can reach you when
        you have no internet, which is why we offer it. To send one we have to keep your
        number in a form we can dial — unlike everywhere else, where it is scrambled and
        cannot be read back. We keep it only while you want reminders, we use it for
        nothing else, and you can ask us to delete it at any time without leaving the
        study.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <strong>Reminder addresses, briefly.</strong> If the system advises you to see a
        health worker, it schedules a reminder — WHO guidance asks for a check-in after one or two
        days. To send that reminder we have to keep your chat address for those one or two
        days. It is deleted the moment the reminder is sent, and it is never kept for
        anyone who has no reminder pending.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Before a message is stored, we automatically remove things that look like phone
        numbers, email addresses, links and identity numbers. This is careful but not
        perfect, so please avoid putting names or numbers of other people in your messages.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Who can see it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The student researcher, the academic supervisor, and clinical reviewers who check
        whether the advice was appropriate. Reviewers see conversations with identifying
        details already removed.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Your messages travel through the messaging service you chose — Telegram or
        WhatsApp — and their own privacy terms apply to that. We do not control them.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        To produce replies, message text is sent to <strong>Anthropic</strong> (the
        language model) and <strong>Voyage AI</strong> (for searching clinical guidance).
        We do not send them your name or your scrambled identifier.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        If Anthropic is unavailable, the same message text may instead be sent to
        <strong>DeepSeek</strong>, so the system can still help you rather than asking you
        to try again later. DeepSeek is based in China, so in that case your message is
        processed outside Nigeria. This happens only when the first service fails, and the
        same safety checks are applied to the reply either way. We still do not send your
        name or your scrambled identifier.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for advertising.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Message transcripts are kept for the duration of the research project and deleted
        afterwards. Summary figures that cannot identify anyone — such as how often the
        system was accurate — may be kept in the final report.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Under the <strong>Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023</strong> you may ask us to show
        you what we hold about you, correct it, or delete it. You may withdraw your consent
        at any time, and doing so will not affect you in any way.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Because we deliberately do not store anything that identifies you, we may need you
        to message us from the same chat so we can find your records.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Contact</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
        <p><strong>Researcher:</strong> Adeola Bada (2024/C/MIT/0127)</p>
        <p><strong>Supervisor:</strong> Prof. Emmanuel Mkpojiogu</p>
        <p><strong>Department:</strong> Information Technology, School of Computing,
           MIVA Open University, Abuja</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
          <!-- TODO before any real participant: add a contact email address here, and the
               research ethics contact if the department requires one. -->
          Contact address to be added before the study opens to participants.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <p class="mt-10 text-center">
    <a href="/register" class="btn-primary">Back to registration</a>
  </p>
</section>
